# Fixed 2026-09-29, defect 130's class, given to defect 133's lane. Symptom:
# a top-level line opened by a word that is not the language's, `recrod
# Point` over its fields, `fucntion f()` over its body, `varaint Shape` over
# its cases, cost `expected_declaration` and dropped its whole indented
# block, every mistake inside it too: the author fixed the word and met them
# in the next run. Cause: the dispatcher's recovery dropped the rest of the
# line and then the block, as it drops a stray one. The block is now read
# by the shape its lines have (`parse/headless.hero`): a `name: type` line
# makes it fields, a name alone on the first line makes it cases, and
# anything else is a body. `expected_declaration` stays the one report of
# the head, whether the word is one edit from a keyword or none, a bare
# name, or followed by junk; a word the lexer refuses with no certain swap
# (`class`) is read the same way under its `reserved_word`.
#
# And a body whose margin holds a tab is read as the body it is, as lane
# 130's third round reads one under any head that failed: `fucntion tabbed()`
# over a tab-indented line costs the tab and the line's own mistake, and no
# second `expected_declaration` for the line the tab left at the margin.

recrod Point  #~ expected_declaration
    x: i64
    y i64  #~ expected_field_type

banana Pair  #~ expected_declaration
    left i64  #~ expected_field_type
    right: i64

Size  #~ expected_declaration
    w: i64
    h i64  #~ expected_field_type

recrod Junk )  #~ expected_declaration
    x: i64
    y i64  #~ expected_field_type

fucntion show()  #~ expected_declaration
    if 1 == 1
        y = 3 )  #~ expected_end_of_line
    z = 4 )  #~ expected_end_of_line

varaint Shape  #~ expected_declaration
    circle
        r f64  #~ expected_field_type
    square

class Holder  #~ reserved_word
    v: i64
    w i64  #~ expected_field_type

fucntion tabbed()  #~ expected_declaration
    y = 3 )  #~ tab_in_indentation expected_end_of_line

function main()
    print(1)

# Read again 2026-10-01, lane recovery-b5 (ruling 5, `selfhost/indent_runs.hero`):
# the tab under `fucntion tabbed()` is laid out as the margin its fix writes,
# four columns, one level under the head, and its `tab_in_indentation` carries
# that fix, certain, which `check --apply` writes (`.applied`).
